      "problem": "Evaluate the indicator function\n$\\mathbf{1}[9 > 7].$",
      "worked_solution": "The indicator function $\\mathbf{1}[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14210051/assets/d223bb71c0ead722dd2318adce354ca32502fe5b08067ff208ee866ed1dc78f5.svg)\n\nHere, the predicate is $9 > 7.$ Since $9$ is greater than $7,$ the predicate is true. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{1}[9 > 7] = 1.\n$$",
